Z||000002||Fformula88||03-13-2001||04:44 PM||||I wasn't a business major but did take some courses.  I found the math end fairly easy (accounting, economics etc etc).  However, I find working with numbers VERY easy.  Many people have a hard time with it.  The management/marketing classes didn't hold my interest too well.  They seemes too much like common sense.  But I was a History major too, so take my opinion with a grain of salt  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> hehe||||reg||1
Z||000003||Hank is Here||03-13-2001||11:18 PM||||I am in business now at Penn State.  Personally I love it.  My major is logistics, which is the movemnt on information, products and money.  Only had one accounting course. Mainly my classes are like transportation,  supply chain, managment, labor studies.  Math isn't that bad, you need to more or less grasp a larger concept or ideal.  It seems in business that equifinity plays a large role--many different ways to the a solution<BR>I like business and the money isn't that bad either!  You have to know how to walk the walk and talk the talk to really be good.  The market for jobs is good too.  I was on a co-op from Jan to August of last year, by June I had an offer from another company that found me for better pay and better location (Belgium) for this summer.   <BR>Email me if you want to ask direct questions.  I am in my 7th of 8 semesters now.   <P>Mark ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula||03-14-2001||07:55 AM||||Thats actually awesome, I go to penn state fayette.  I know I can handle the math, I'm really good with numbers up to stuff like advanced calculus then it stops being logical.  and I've always liked to watch the stock market.  I'm pretty sure I'm going to switch next year.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cheever2||03-14-2001||10:18 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>Im going into this one blind.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>I know for a fact employers cannot discriminate just because of that unless it has a direct affect on your ability to do the job.  But you sound like you're very accomplished.  Actually, you could probably do much better at business than in electronics.  Most of the management I ever worked for were blind metaphorically speaking.<P>How do you do this Forum stuff?  I mean, do you have one of those text-to-yak (TTY) translator things?<P>Also, how many Fieros do you have?  Do you have someone drive you around once in a while?<P>Lastly, I too am good with numbers.  Up to around 100. <BR>||||reg||6
