Z||000009||Eric_PA||03-16-2001||07:52 PM||||I switched my major a couple of times and delayed my graduation. I went from Electronics Technology to an Engineering program, then back to Electronics Technology. I finally graduated from the Electronics program and will be transfering into a 2 + 2 program for Electro mechanical Engineering at Penn State next Fall. I guess that isn't much of a jump though. They are related I guess. I have got to say, the industrial world in Electronics has treated me very well so far, especially with a programming background. Check the papers, they are always looking for C programers or PLC programming along with embeded controler experience.<P>I guess I'm just trying talk you into statying with Electronics.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Eric||||reg||6
Z||000010||Cheever2||03-17-2001||07:40 PM||||Can you business majors explain one thing for me...<BR>why is it Management can't go for very long before they put some <I>sign</I> up over everybody's heads?  What is it that makes them do that?  Is it actually taught in those college classes?<P>Motivational signs have a way of making me <B>lose</B> morale (and my breakfast).  I work best in a tastefully decorated environment, with plants, family photos, wilderness pictures that make you think of places <I>away</I> from work, a little humor, and of course Fiero calendars.  Signs that seem to shout at me don't do the trick.<BR> <BR>||||reg||6
